{
 "id": "Cigarette",
 "slug": "cigarette",
 "topic": "How the cigarette was invented (story Reel drawn on cigarette paper: ink silhouettes, ember orange, living smoke)",
 "title": [
  "WHO INVENTED",
  "THE CIGARETTE"
 ],
 "accent": "CIGARETTE",
 "voice": {
  "id": "Bj9UqZbhQsanLzgalpEG",
  "model": "eleven_v4",
  "language": "en",
  "settings": {
   "stability": 0.45,
   "similarity_boost": 0.8,
   "style": 0.35,
   "use_speaker_boost": true
  }
 },
 "tail": 2.0,
 "lead": 2,
 "gap": 0.14,
 "tempo": 1.06,
 "script": [
  {
   "beat": "s",
   "text": "The cigarette was invented by beggars. Digging through the trash."
  },
  {
   "beat": "s",
   "text": "This ain't some bedtime story, buddy. Let me roll it out for ya."
  },
  {
   "beat": "s",
   "text": "A thousand years ago, the Maya were already smoking tobacco, rolled up in leaves. For their gods."
  },
  {
   "beat": "s",
   "text": "Fourteen ninety-two. Columbus's crew sees it. And one sailor carries the habit home to Spain."
  },
  {
   "beat": "s",
   "text": "Folks see smoke pouring out of his mouth, and figure he's got the devil in him. Story goes, they locked him up."
  },
  {
   "beat": "s",
   "text": "But the rich fellas loved it. Big fat cigars. And they tossed the butts in the street."
  },
  {
   "beat": "s",
   "text": "And in Seville, the beggars picked up those butts, shredded them, and rolled them in scraps of paper."
  },
  {
   "beat": "s",
   "text": "A poor man's cigar. The French called it a cigarette. A little cigar."
  },
  {
   "beat": "s",
   "text": "Soldiers carried it around the world. But every one was still rolled by hand. Four a minute, if you were quick."
  },
  {
   "beat": "s",
   "text": "Then, eighteen eighty. A fella named Bonsack builds a machine. A hundred and twenty thousand a day."
  },
  {
   "beat": "s",
   "text": "You get it, buddy? I said, you get it? Like opening a fire hydrant."
  },
  {
   "beat": "s",
   "text": "And here's the part nobody rolled into the paper. Today, tobacco kills more than eight million people a year. That's real."
  },
  {
   "beat": "s",
   "text": "So next time you see a butt on the sidewalk, remember. That's where it all started."
  },
  {
   "beat": "s",
   "text": "That's about it, folks. Follow for more strange history. See ya!"
  }
 ],
 "science": [
  {
   "claim": "Seville beggars rolled discarded cigar scraps in paper (papeletes), 17th century",
   "note": "widely told origin; hedge as the common account"
  },
  {
   "claim": "Bonsack machine (patent 1880-81): about 120,000 cigarettes a day",
   "note": "vs about 4 a minute by a skilled hand roller"
  },
  {
   "claim": "Tobacco kills more than 8 million people a year",
   "note": "WHO"
  },
  {
   "claim": "Rodrigo de Jerez jailed by the Inquisition for smoking",
   "note": "traditional story, hedged with \"story goes\""
  }
 ],
